// Chronicle rules: the activities
// -------------------------------
// Imported by windows.pg (the game's run for the activities and the doors), forecast.pg and
// epitaph.pg. Never loaded itself.
// Input:  `age` (years), `character` (a table of stats and flags), `done` (a table: activity id
//         -> the terms already completed; an activity never done has no key), `activityId` (""
//         for every activity; the forecast's one id, to shape that one only), `world` (months
//         since the world's Year 0: the date a closing is written with), `running` (the id of
//         the activity he is at, "" for none), `lives` (the lives lived in this world, this one
//         counted: 1 is a first life, which opens on one task and is shown the others one at a
//         time). `character` also carries the town, which is the world's and not his:
//         "town_known" (1 once a life has explored it), "town.<place id>" (the place's level) and
//         "fund.<place id>" (the coin left to the place by lives that ended), as towntable.pg says.
// Output: `activities`, one table per thing the character may spend months doing, in the order
//         the Life screen lists them:
//           id, group, name, glyph, months, rank ("" or caps), each ("" or caps), path ("" or the
//           path it belongs to, `paths` below), enters (true for the activity that makes him one
//           of a path), board (true when it feeds him), fromAge, finishBy,
//           gains [{stat, amount, label, name}] (at term; label: the stat's short name, for a
//           row; name: its full one, for a gloss),
//           costs [{stat, amount, label, name}] (taken when it begins),
//           requires [{stat, label, current, needed, room, cost}] (current: the character's;
//           flat: eased and anyOf are weighed here and not passed on; `cost` marks what is one
//           of its costs, `room` what is room for a gain: neither is written on a tile),
//           needs (the requirements as the table writes them, with their eased and anyOf: for
//           the tools, tools/chronicle_graph.pg; the screen reads `requires`),
//           locked (true while a requirement is unmet),
//           done (the terms completed), uses (0 = as often as he likes), left (-1 = no limit),
//           spent (true once a limited activity has no use left),
//           closed (true once it can no longer finish by its `finishBy`),
//           pathOpen (true while its path is his, or open to him),
//           reach (0-100: how much of what it asks he has, on average),
//           listed (true while the screen has a row for it: its path open, neither spent nor
//           closed, he is of the age it shows from, has its share of what it asks and, in a
//           first life, has done the terms it shows after),
//           showAge, showFrom, showAfter, firstLife (what it is listed by, as below),
//           tally (how often it was done and, for a limited one, what is left, as the row
//           writes it: "DONE 2", "DONE 0 · 1 LEFT"),
//           place ("" or the place of the town it is done at: the Town page lists it there, not
//           the Life page), raises and level ("" and 0, or the place its term raises and the level
//           it raises it to), yearMonths (0, or the months of his life it takes at once when it
//           begins: its `years`), goto ("" or the page that confirming it opens, and nothing else),
//           until ("" or when it closes, as the row writes it: "CLOSES 5/11", the world's date
//           (month/year) of the last month he may begin it, or "CLOSES THIS MONTH"; said from
//           `closingShown` months before it), urgent (true from `closingUrgent` months before),
//           after (its steps, as below).
//
// `months: 0` is an activity done at once: it takes no time, and can be done while another runs.
//
// Optional fields of an activity:
//   fromAge: N       he may begin it from that age (default 7). Younger, it asks for the age.
//   showAge: N       its row is listed from that age (default `fromAge`): before he may begin
//                    it, it stands locked, the age the first thing it asks.
//   showFrom: N      its row is listed once he has that much (in percent) of what it asks
//                    (default `reachShown`); 0 lists it whatever he has.
//                    The great step of each age (the way into a path, its proving, its mastery)
//                    carries both: it shows ahead, whatever he has, so he knows what the years
//                    he is in lead to. A proving and a mastery show from the milestone before;
//                    the three ways into a path show from his first day, locked: they are what
//                    a childhood is spent toward.
//   showAfter: N     in a first life (`lives` 1), its row is listed once N terms in all are done
//                    in this life, whatever else lists it: the list grows one task at a time
//                    while the guide (achievements.pg) walks him through it. From the second
//                    life it is ignored.
//   firstLife: true  the opening task: listed only in a first life that has done nothing yet.
//                    A later life never has its row, nor does a first life once any term is
//                    done.
//   finishBy: N      its term must fall at that age or before (default lib.pg's `lastAge`): an
//                    activity of 18 months with finishBy 25 is begun by 23.5 at the latest.
//                    lib.pg's `anyAge` for what old age does not close.
//   board: true      meals provided: a month at it takes no ration and costs no Vitality, held
//                    rations or not (resources.pg).
//   path, enters     a path's activities are listed once he is one of it (holds its flag); the
//                    one that enters it is listed until he is one of any. The paths exclude
//                    each other. The page says "class" for what the rules call a path.
//   lastResort: true an `enters` that is only for who missed every other one: it has no row
//                    while another way into a class can still be begun, nor while he is at one
//                    (`running`), nor once he is of a class. It is listed from the month the
//                    last of the others closes.
//   opens: "text"    what the log and a toast say the month its row comes into the list, in
//                    place of the "New: ..." every new row gets.
//   costs: [{stat, amount}]
//                    what it takes from him when it begins. He must hold that much to begin (it
//                    is listed in `requires`).
//   amount           every {stat, amount} of an activity (its gains, its costs, a bonus step's
//                    gains and `more`, an `after` step's gains and effects) may leave the
//                    amount out: it is 1. {stat: "arms"} brings, or takes, one.
//   uses: N          it can be done N times, then it is spent.
//   requires: [{stat, needed}]
//                    what he must hold to begin it. `needed` is 1 when the entry gives none:
//                    {stat: "letters"} asks that he has any. An entry may carry:
//     label: "text"           what the row calls it, in place of the stat's name.
//     eased: {flag, needed, at}   with the flag held (at `at` or more: 1 when it gives none), it
//                             asks `needed` instead. A list of them: the least of those that hold.
//                             Its `needed` is always written: it is what the entry is eased to.
//     anyOf: [flag]           one of the flags is enough: current is 1 when he holds any.
//   bonus: [step]    what changes with a stat he holds, or with the town. A step is
//                    {stat, needed, ...}: with the stat at `needed` or more (1 when the step
//                    gives none) it replaces the activity's own gains, months, rank, each, uses,
//                    fromAge, showAge, showFrom, finishBy, board or path with the ones it gives,
//                    and adds its `more` [{stat, amount}] to what the term brings. Every step
//                    that holds is applied, in order: the last one wins what two of them give.
//   featured: true   the page wants it seen: its tile stands on a gold ground while he can
//                    choose it (exploring the town, which a life should not miss).
//   major: true      it turns his life (a class, the town): its tile is framed in gold and shows
//                    its mark, in every state.
//   about: "text"    what it does, and a line of the town's own, said under its name in its gloss
//                    in the place of its group.
//   whileNot: "stat" its row is not listed once he holds that stat ("town_known": exploring the
//                    town is for who does not know it).
//   place: "id"      it is done at a place of the town: once the town is known its row stands on
//                    the Town page, at that place (the market), and no longer on the Life page.
//                    So does a work that raises a place (`raises`): it stands under the places.
//   goto: "page"     confirming it opens that page ("town") and does nothing else: no term, no
//                    month, no line.
//   raises: "id", level: N
//                    its term raises that place of the town to level N. It is listed only while
//                    the place is one level below, once the town is known, and while the place
//                    is on the Town page for him (lib.pg's `placeShown`: the town grows with
//                    what he does). The works that
//                    raise a place are not written here: they are made from towntable.pg.
//   years: N         it takes N years of his life at once when it begins, on top of its months.
//
// An activity that brings a stat with a limit (lib.pg's `statLimits`) asks for room for it: one
// more requirement, {stat, label "Room for Rations", current (the room left), needed 1, room
// true}, after its costs. Full, it is locked; begun with any room left, it brings all it brings,
// past the limit if need be.
//   after: [step]    what changes with repetition. A step is {uses: N, ...}:
//                      rank, months, gains   replace the activity's own once N terms are done
//                                            (the last step reached wins);
//                      effects [{stat, amount}], entry "text"
//                                            happen once, at the term that makes it N
//                                            (forecast.pg applies them).
//
// No function here: lib.pg holds them all, ahead of every table (see there why).
//
// The numbers are the balance of res/chronicle/chronicle-balance (tasks.json): change them here,
// nothing in C++ moves. Buy Silence ("silence") is a stub: nothing comes after the robbery yet for
// silence to quiet; it is kept as the place a Guild's pursuit will hang from.

import "string"
import "math"
import "algorithm"
import "lib"
import "towntable"

var errors = []

// A row is listed once he has, on average, this much (in percent) of what it asks: each
// requirement counts its share up to 100, costs and room are left out (they are bought, not
// grown). Further from it, the row stays hidden, so a boy is not shown a life of locked rows:
// the three ways into a path are the only ones he sees from the start (`showFrom: 0`), and the
// doors on the clock say what else is coming.
var reachShown = 75

// What a `bonus` step may replace of its activity
var bonusFields = ["gains", "months", "rank", "each", "uses", "fromAge", "showAge", "showFrom", "finishBy", "board", "path"]

// A row says when it closes once he has this many months left to begin it, or fewer, and says it
// as urgent from the second: so no row leaves the list without having said so.
var closingShown = 24
var closingUrgent = 6

// The paths a life may take, which the page calls his class: the flag that makes him one of it.
// The renegade's is the one left to who took none of the three in time
var paths = [
    {id: "warrior", name: "The Keep", flag: "keep_oath"},
    {id: "mage", name: "The Collegium", flag: "collegium"},
    {id: "thief", name: "The Hidden Hand", flag: "hidden_hand"},
    {id: "renegade", name: "The Greenwood", flag: "renegade"}
]

var activities = [
    // The opening of a first life: one month that costs nothing and brings the first thing he
    // holds. It leaves the list once done
    {id: "helping", group: "Work", name: "Start Helping Out", glyph: "work", months: 1, rank: "", each: "AT THE MILL", path: "", fromAge: 6,
     board: true, uses: 1, firstLife: true,
     gains: [{stat: "rations", amount: 12}],
     requires: []},
    {id: "carters", group: "Work", name: "Carry for the Carters", glyph: "work", months: 3, rank: "", each: "MEALS PROVIDED", path: "", board: true, showAfter: 1,
     gains: [{stat: "coin", amount: 6}],
     requires: []},
    {id: "mill", group: "Work", name: "Help at the Mill", glyph: "work", months: 6, rank: "", each: "", path: "", showAfter: 3,
     gains: [{stat: "str"}, {stat: "vit"}, {stat: "coin", amount: 8}],
     requires: [],
     after: [{uses: 2, months: 9, gains: [{stat: "coin", amount: 6}]}],
     bonus: [{stat: "town.mill", more: [{stat: "coin", amount: 4}]}]},
    {id: "messages", group: "Work", name: "Run Messages", glyph: "town", months: 3, rank: "", each: "", path: "", showAfter: 2,
     gains: [{stat: "dex"}, {stat: "coin", amount: 3}],
     requires: [],
     after: [{uses: 2, gains: [{stat: "coin", amount: 5}]}]},
    // What feeds him until the market is his to buy at: meals while he is at it, and rations to
    // take away
    {id: "kitchen", group: "Work", name: "Help in the Kitchen", glyph: "trade", months: 3, rank: "", each: "MEALS PROVIDED", path: "", board: true, showAfter: 3,
     gains: [{stat: "rations", amount: 6}],
     requires: []},
    {id: "market", group: "Work", name: "Help at the Market", glyph: "trade", months: 6, rank: "", each: "", path: "", fromAge: 8, showAfter: 5,
     gains: [{stat: "guile"}, {stat: "coin", amount: 8}],
     requires: [],
     after: [{uses: 2, gains: [{stat: "coin", amount: 12}]}]},
    {id: "smithy", group: "Work", name: "Work the Smithy", glyph: "forge", months: 9, rank: "", each: "", path: "", fromAge: 9,
     gains: [{stat: "str"}, {stat: "coin", amount: 18}],
     requires: [{stat: "str", needed: 8}],
     bonus: [{stat: "town.smithy", fromAge: 8}, {stat: "town.smithy", needed: 3, more: [{stat: "coin", amount: 6}]}]},
    {id: "night", group: "Work", name: "Work the Night Market", glyph: "trade", months: 6, rank: "", each: "", path: "", fromAge: 13, finishBy: 18, uses: 2,
     gains: [{stat: "guile"}, {stat: "coin", amount: 12}],
     requires: [{stat: "guile"}],
     after: [{uses: 2, effects: [{stat: "night_contacts"}], entry: "The night market knows his face"}]},

    // What is bought on the spot is bought in town: once the town is known these stand on its
    // page, at the market, and the Life page keeps one tile that goes there
    {id: "goto.market", group: "Market", name: "Go to the Market", glyph: "town", months: 0, rank: "", each: "IN TOWN", path: "", finishBy: anyAge, showFrom: 100,
     goto: "town",
     gains: [],
